      "side": 1,
      "message": "@matthias.sohn@gmail.com, unfortunately not all lucene activity is visible via logging. The low-level API operations (such as flushing, merging, committing, etc) are logged through the `InforStream` interface [1][2].\n\nWe could use `JavaLoggingInfoStream` [3], but that would require **also** to bridge JUL to log4j, and I don\u0027t think it will be necessary, since we can just provide an alternative log4j implementation, as @danielesassoli@gmail.com has done with this change.\n\nWDYT? @luca.milanesio@gmail.com @matthias.sohn@gmail.com\n\n\n[1] https://github.com/apache/lucene/blob/main/lucene/core/src/java/org/apache/lucene/util/InfoStream.java#L30.\n\n[2] https://github.com/apache/lucene/blob/main/lucene/core/src/java/org/apache/lucene/index/IndexWriter.java#L4262\n[3] https://github.com/apache/lucene/blob/main/lucene/core/src/java/org/apache/lucene/util/JavaLoggingInfoStream.java",
      "parentUuid": "6542489c_b858698f",
      "revId": "6e3735df2db87f5d2989a191bee990d701ce9ec7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
